(3) REST API Plan

----------NOTES----------

//An API is a way for two pieces of software to communicate.
//REST is a set of conventions for communicating with a web service using HTTP requests.
//A REST API call is simply your application sending a request to Firebase.

Method |Purpose |SkillsTrack example
GET |Retrieve data |Get a learner's tasks
POST |Create new data |Create a booking
PUT |Replace/write data |Save a user's information
PATCH |Update part of existing data |Change a task to completed
DELETE |Remove data |Delete a task

(3.1) Users Endpoints

Create User
POST /users
Purpose:
Save new user profile after registration.

Read User
GET /users/{userId}
Purpose:
Load learner profile.

Update User
PUT /users/{userId}
Purpose:
Update profile information.

Delete User
DELETE /users/{userId}
Purpose:
Remove user account.

(3.2) Tasks Endpoints

Load Tasks
GET /tasks/{userId}
Purpose:
Retrieve learner tasks.

Create Task
POST /tasks
Purpose:
Add new task.

Update Task
PUT /tasks/{taskId}
Purpose:
Change task information or status.

Delete Task
DELETE /tasks/{taskId}
Purpose:
Remove task.

(3.3) Support Booking Endpoints

Retrieve Bookings
GET /bookings/{userId}
Purpose:
View learner bookings.

Create Booking
POST /bookings
Purpose:
Create support request.

Update Booking
PUT /bookings/{bookingId}
Purpose:
Modify booking status.

Delete Booking
DELETE /bookings/{bookingId}
Purpose:
Cancel booking.

(3.4) Resource Endpoints

Get Resources
GET /resources
Purpose:
Load learning resources.

Add Resource
POST /resources
Purpose:
Add new learning material.

Update Resource
PUT /resources/{resourceId}
Purpose:
Edit resource details.

Delete Resource
DELETE /resources/{resourceId}
Purpose:
Remove resource.

(4) Security Planning

Security Rules:
Users can only view their own tasks.
Users can only edit their own bookings.
Assessors can view all bookings.
Firebase Authentication manages sign-in security.

Conclusion

The proposed Firebase database structure provides organised storage for learners, tasks, bookings, scores and resources. The planned REST endpoints support full CRUD functionality and will simplify development of the SkillsTrack Learner Support Portal during Month 2. The design also supports security, scalability and efficient data retrieval.
